WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.130
How can we stop messing
with the climate?

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.480
To start answering this question, it's
useful to break the carbon climate

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.950
problem into four components--
emissions, concentrations,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:13.730
climate change, and climate impacts.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:18.680
First, the emission of carbon dioxide
and other long-lived greenhouse gases

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.540
that can alter the climate.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:24.800
Emissions are the human-caused flow
of greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.890
They're typically measured in tons of
carbon dioxide equivalent per year.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.870
Total global emissions
are about 40 billion tons

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:36.070
per year, the weight of 40
cubic kilometers of water.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.200
In personal terms, that's
about 5 and 1/2 tons

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.840
per year per person on average.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.400
But we are not all equal contributors.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.450
Given how much I fly, I'm responsible
for about 30 tons per year,

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.520
whereas a typical member of
the poorest billion humans

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.670
is responsible for only
1/10 of a ton per year.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:01.210
Here is how global emissions have
been growing over the last century.

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.330
What you see is accelerating
growth with a few pauses

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.120
during times where the
global economy faltered.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.350
There is no evidence of a slowdown
over the decade since 1992,

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:16.360
when the world first made formal
commitments to work together to cut

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.180
emissions to protect our climate.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.530
Second, the concentrations of
greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.380
This is the amount of carbon dioxide
gas in the atmosphere at any one time.

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:29.830
We care about this,
because it's the amount

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:33.860
of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere
that is what most directly causes

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.990
climate change at any given time.

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:41.670
Here is how global concentrations have
been growing over the last century.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:46.330
You see very steady growth
with a slow, even acceleration.

